# Recomputable from the code plus the data, and large. `results/` is already covered by the
# repo-level .gitignore; these two are specific to this subdirectory.
#
# NOTE: gitignore has no trailing comments -- "cache/   # why" is a pattern with a comment in
# it, matching nothing. Comments get their own line.

# per-split row attributes, rebuilt by pool_attributes.py in ~40 s per split
cache/

# one log per split per run
logs/

# The derived tables under diagnosis/ ARE kept: they are the numbers PROPOSAL.md cites, they are
# small, and a reader should not have to re-run 100 split-jobs to check a figure in the text.
# The figures themselves are covered by the repo-level *.png rule.
